AB  -  INTERVENTION: Intervention1: Durvalumab: Patients will be randomized in a 1:1 ratio to receive either durvalumab plus platinum‐based chemotherapy before surgery followed by durvalumab post‐surgery or placebo plus platinum‐based chemotherapy before surgery followed by placebo post‐surgery. Control Intervention1: Placebo plus Chemotherapy: Patients will be randomized in a 1:1 ratio to receive either durvalumab plus platinum‐based chemotherapy before surgery followed by durvalumab post‐surgery or placebo plus platinum‐based chemotherapy before surgery followed by placebo post‐surgery. CONDITION: Malignant neoplasm of unspecifiedpart of bronchus or lung PRIMARY OUTCOME: To assess the activity of durvalumab + chemotherapy administered prior to surgery compared with placebo + chemotherapy administered prior to surgery in terms of mPR. ; i). mPR (10% or less residual viable tumor tissue in lung primary tumor after neoadjuvant treatment at the time of resection) in FAS ; Timepoint: Overall Survival (OS) (Time frame‐Approximately 5 years) SECONDARY OUTCOME: 1. To assess the activity of durvalumab plus chemotherapy administered prior to surgery compared with placebo plus chemotherapy administered prior to surgery in terms of pCR ; i). pCR (absence of any residual viable tumor in the primary lung lesion and lymph nodes at the time of surgical resection) in FAS and PD‐L1‐TCÃ¢?Â¥1% patients ; Timepoint: Overall Survival (OS) (Time frame‐Approximately 5 years) 2. To assess the activity of durvalumab plus chemotherapy administered prior to surgery compared with placebo plus chemotherapy administered prior to surgery in terms of mPR ; i). .mPR in PD‐L1‐TCÃ¢?Â¥1% patientsTimepoint: Overall Survival (OS) (Time frame‐Approximately 5 years) 2.To assess the activity of durvalumab plus chemotherapy administered prior to surgery compared with placebo plus chemotherapy administered prior to surgery in terms of mPR assessed according to the immune‐related pathologic response criteria