AB  -  Pembrolizumab is a humanized monoclonal antibody against PD‐1 capable of enhancing antitumor immune activity. The KEYNOTE‐001 study showed that pembrolizumab has activity in advanced non‐small‐cell lung cancer patients and identified programmed death ligand 1 (PD‐L1) as a companion test to select patients most likely to benefit from pembrolizumab. Five randomized clinical trials showed the efficacy of pembrolizumab in non‐small‐cell lung cancer: in second‐line setting PD‐L1 ≥1% (KEYNOTE‐010), in first‐line setting PD‐L1 ≥50% (KEYNOTE‐024 and KEYNOTE‐042) and in first‐line setting in combination with platinum doublets, any expression of PD‐L1 (KEYNOTE‐189 and KEYNOTE‐407). Future challenges are the identification of the role of pembrolizumab in adjuvant, neoadjuvant, locally advanced disease or oncogene‐addicted patients, in combination with radiotherapy or other biological agents.
